               <history>
                  <provenance type="#rejected"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_470">Romsey, Hampshire,
                        Abbey of Saint Mary the Virgin and St Elfleda, of Benedictine
                        nuns</orgName><p>The Romsey attribution was rejected in the second edition
                        of Medieval Libraries of Great Britain (1964), with no folio references
                        specified. No changes to the Romsey attribution were made in the Supplement
                        (1987). During data reconciliation in 2026, no corresponding index card was
                        found. It is worth noting, though, that the rejected Romsey card for London,
                        British Library, Additional MS 28188 has the following note at the top:
                        'Reject, and reject also Cotton Vit. A. vii'.</p></provenance>
               </history>
               <additional>
                  <adminInfo>
                     <recordHist>
